{"title":"2011 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/d/e9d2c9b1c09c1f9eeefa3f249cd7d5ddfbbff67d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A = \\left\\{ 2,5,10,17,\\cdots,n^2+1,\\cdots\\right\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"261\" height=\"22\" /> be the set of all positive squares plus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/2/392a60e898818c73b02420c2c40ee5c0fe7136b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B = \\left\\{101, 104, 109, 116,\\cdots,m^2 + 100,\\cdots\\right\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"340\" height=\"22\" /> be the set of all positive squares plus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e59e2c6e83eb78cca610a5fd4070ae01c8d4ae60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>(a) What is the smallest number in both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p>(b) Find all numbers that are in both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The smallest number in both sets is 101. This is because it is both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/2/d32ccbffce2911b201a664cd608099234f7ed782.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1^2+100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"65\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/0/6a0820b09be57820d447dda06efadacdbe3e8c18.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10^2+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"56\" height=\"16\" />. Subtracting 10-1 gives us 9. This means that all other numbers in both sets must be less than 9 apart, because squares get further apart the bigger they get. Following a geometric sequence gives us 9,3,1 so the squares must be that far apart. This means the next term is 325, because it is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/0/2202d6dca0ba6aba29d5d46d586fa7fc8678ada9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15^2+100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"74\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/7/e076f34b9390c89144a713017b78a75bf7bc720b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$18^2+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"56\" height=\"16\" />. There is only one left, which is 2501, because it is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/2/4e2c8aef73c6143e105a816204f392c6678454b4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$49^2+100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"74\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/9/049fd5f9fac015ca0b7b1f1a373bf2d0dc07b5a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$50^2+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"56\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_UNCO_Math_Contest_II\" title=\"2011 UNCO Math Contest II\">2011 UNCO Math Contest II</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems\" title=\"2011 UNCO Math Contest II Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Answer_Key\" title=\"2011 UNCO Math Contest II Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://uncmathcontest.wordpress.com/\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2011 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2011 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2011 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wi